The tuples and binding terms also match.

The unqualified cubic claim fails outside the diagonal. In the note’s illustrative \(C_\gamma=20\) model, take
\[
\tau=(3,1/100,3/10),\qquad
\tau'=(23/20,1/100,3/10).
\]
The three DL terms are
\[
9,\qquad6.42,\qquad[8.344211321,\;8.344215053].
\]
Here **\(3a\) binds strictly**. C25(i) itself remains correct.

These are identities between derived upper-bound expressions, not lower bounds on actual DL complexity.

**6. Scope and literature**

The §7 conclusion—**a cheap individual-log phase is not established**—is justified. Saturation of the whole lattice does not force its projection onto new coordinates to have index coprime to \(p-1\). This does not establish an impossibility theorem for precomputation.

The negative conclusion in §8 is also justified: the prime-field algorithm does not transfer as written. Its positive injectivity assertion needs qualification. For example, in \(\mathbb Q(\sqrt2)\), let
\[
u=3+\sqrt2,\quad v=5+2\sqrt2,\quad \varepsilon=3+2\sqrt2.
\]
Then
\[
(\varepsilon u,\varepsilon v)=(13+9\sqrt2,\;23+16\sqrt2)
\]
is a different pair with the same ratio. Both pairs have coprime principal ideals of norms \(7,17\), and their cross-product difference is zero. Unit normalization and principality issues remain after the norm argument.

For KW, putting \(t=\log Q\) gives exactly the stated expansion
\[
\log T=
\left(\frac{2c(1-\beta)}{\log2}+o(1)\right)
t^\beta(\log t)^{2-\beta}.
\]
Thus it is \(L_Q[\beta+o(1)]\), rather than \(L_Q[\beta,C]\). The comparisons at \(\beta=2/5\) and \(1/2\) are correct. [Kleinjung–Wesolowski, Theorem 1.1](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1906.10668)

The literature’s “nothing found” wording is appropriately a search result. It should explicitly concern classical algorithms and use quantitative characteristic ranges instead of “only small characteristic.”

Verification: all **8 repository tests passed**. Independent scratch checks confirmed four exhaustive split identities, 144 hidden-label cases, 108 exact diagonal interval identities, and the mixed-tuple counterexample. The repository was left unchanged; [scratch checks](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/dlog25_2/adversarial_checks.py) and [parameter output](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/dlog25_2/params_check.txt) are available.